    "facts": "Thereafter, on 07.01.2024 and 10.01.2024 he not only raped her,\nbut also made a video and, thereafter, threatened to make it viral and to kill the complainant.\nOn this intimation, crime was registered on the very same date at police station Bahodapur, District Gwalior bearing Crime No.469/2024 for the offences punishable under Sections 376, 377, 323, 294, 506, 34 of IPC.\n",
    "arguments": "The allegation against the applicant is of 376 and 377 of IPC and the offence under said section is not made out against the present applicant as the present applicant and prosecutrix are husband and wife.\nThe FIR is delayed by approximately six months and no satisfactory explanation has been given by the prosecutrix/complainant.\nSuch inordinate delay in lodging the FIR points towards the fact that it was registered after post deliberations, consultation and discussions of prosecutrix with her family members and after taking legal advice, as would be evident from the F.I.R. that at the time of submitting complaint, the complainant was accompanied with her counsel just to harass the present applicant.\nThe FIR got registered after the divorce notices were sent to the prosecutrix/complainant by her husband/co-accused Sadik on 27.04.2024, 29.05.2024 and 01.07.2024 respectively.\nUnder these circumstances, the applicant prays for anticipatory bail.\nFurther, as per the allegations family members of applicant had taken obscene photos of complainant and had threatened her of defaming.\nSince investigation is still going on, the applicant doesn't deserves to be granted anticipatory bail.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "After hearing counsels for the parties and taking over all facts and circumstances of FIR, 161 and 164 Statements, this Court finds strength in the arguments advance by the counsels for the respondents and observes that the case of the present applicant being husband is different from that of the co-accused who had been granted bail.\nThus, in view of the above observations, no case of grant of anticipatory bail is made out in favor of the present applicant.\n",
    "decision": "13. Accordingly, the present application is hereby dismissed.\n"
